# Travel Guardian Environment Configuration Example

# Frontend (Google Maps Platform API Key for Places Autocomplete, Geocoding & Directions/Routing)
# Expected to be client-accessible in browser, but MUST be restricted in Google Cloud Console:
# 1. API Enablement:
#    - Maps JavaScript API
#    - Places API (New & Classic Autocomplete)
#    - Geocoding API
#    - Directions API (Routes / Directions Service)
# 2. Application Restrictions (HTTP Referrers):
#    - http://localhost:3000/*
#    - http://127.0.0.1:3000/*
#    - https://your-production-domain.com/*
# 3. Billing:
#    - Valid Google Cloud billing account associated with project to avoid OVER_QUERY_LIMIT
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_maps_api_key_here

# Frontend (Public token for Mapbox GL JS map tiles rendering)
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_mapbox_public_token_here

# Backend / Server (API Key for Google Gemini Generative AI)
# Stored securely on server-side, never exposed to client bundles
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Backend Service URL (optional if running FastAPI backend)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
